### Documentation: Frappe Custom HTML Block Calendar

This documentation describes the implementation of a custom calendar HTML block for integration into a Frappe framework application. It includes HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code for a fully functional calendar with navigable months and day-click functionality. 

---

### 1. **HTML Structure**

```html
<div id="custom-calendar">
    <div id="calendar-header">
        <button id="prev-month">&lt;</button>
        <span id="month-year"></span>
        <button id="next-month">&gt;</button>
    </div>
    <div id="calendar-days"></div>
</div>
```

#### Explanation:
- **`custom-calendar`**: The main container for the calendar.
- **`calendar-header`**: Contains navigation buttons (`prev-month` and `next-month`) and displays the current month and year.
- **`calendar-days`**: A grid container for rendering the days of the month.

---

### 2. **CSS Styling**

```css
#custom-calendar {
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: auto;
    text-align: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}

#calendar-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
}

#calendar-days {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr);
    gap: 5px;
}

.calendar-day {
    padding: 10px;
    border: 1px solid #ddd;
    border-radius: 5px;
    text-align: center;
    cursor: pointer;
}

.calendar-day.today {
    background-color: #f0f8ff;
    font-weight: bold;
}

.calendar-day:hover {
    background-color: #e6f7ff;
}
```

#### Explanation:
- The calendar grid uses `grid-template-columns` to create a 7-column layout for the days of the week.
- **`calendar-day.today`** highlights the current date.
- Hover effects enhance interactivity.

